From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: tegra: dfll: Stop CPU speedo 2 at 2014.5 MHz for the
 SHIELD TV 2017

The DFLL builds its OPP table, and so cpufreq's rates, up to
tegra210_cpu_max_freq_table[speedo_id]. For speedo 2 that is 2218.5 MHz,
above the 2014.5 MHz the SHIELD TV 2017's (SKU 0x87) stock kernel uses.
Stop there too. It was brought up in stages, 1020 and 1912.5 MHz first
(NOTES.md).

Speedo 2 may not be the SHIELD's alone, so this stays a darcy patch.
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
index 457a77c5b..a4a20d7d2 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra124-dfll-fcpu.c
@@ -175,7 +175,11 @@ static const struct cvb_table tegra124_cpu_cvb_tables[] = {
 static const unsigned long tegra210_cpu_max_freq_table[] = {
 	[0] = 1912500000UL,
 	[1] = 1912500000UL,
-	[2] = 2218500000UL,
+	/*
+	 * The SHIELD TV 2017 (SKU 0x87) is speedo 2: stop where its stock
+	 * kernel does.
+	 */
+	[2] = 2014500000UL,
 	[3] = 1785000000UL,
 	[4] = 1632000000UL,
 	[5] = 1912500000UL,
